<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>FYA Practice Stations — Clinical Informatics STP</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&family=DM+Sans:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;1,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
:root{
  --bg:#f7f6f2;--surface:#fff;--surface2:#f0efe9;--surface3:#e8e7e0;
  --border:rgba(0,0,0,0.09);--border2:rgba(0,0,0,0.18);
  --text:#1a1917;--muted:#5c5b53;--hint:#9e9d96;
  --radius:10px;--radius-lg:14px;
  --reading:#185FA5;--reading-bg:#E6F1FB;
  --station:#0F6E56;--station-bg:#E1F5EE;
  --warn:#BA7517;--danger:#A32D2D;
  --prof:#4a3fa0;--prof-bg:#eeecfd;
  --ds:#0f6e56;--ds-bg:#e1f5ee;
  --sys:#1557a0;--sys-bg:#e6f0fb;
  --pol:#7a4a0a;--pol-bg:#faeeda;
  --dh:#7a2510;--dh-bg:#faece7;
  --ai:#7a2040;--ai-bg:#fbeaf0;
}
@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){
  :root{
    --bg:#181714;--surface:#222120;--surface2:#2a2927;--surface3:#333230;
    --border:rgba(255,255,255,0.09);--border2:rgba(255,255,255,0.2);
    --text:#f0efe9;--muted:#a8a79f;--hint:#6b6960;
    --reading:#7ab8f0;--reading-bg:#0a2440;
    --station:#5dcaa5;--station-bg:#0a3028;
    --warn:#f0b860;--danger:#f08070;
    --prof:#b0a8f0;--prof-bg:#2a2660;
    --ds:#5dcaa5;--ds-bg:#0a3028;
    --sys:#7ab8f0;--sys-bg:#0a2440;
    --pol:#f0b860;--pol-bg:#3a2808;
    --dh:#f08870;--dh-bg:#3a1408;
    --ai:#f090b0;--ai-bg:#3a0e22;
  }
}
*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0;-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent}
html{font-size:16px;scroll-behavior:smooth}
body{font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);min-height:100vh;padding-bottom:4rem}

/* ── NAV ── */
nav{background:var(--surface);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.75rem 1rem;position:sticky;top:0;z-index:200;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem}
.nav-title{font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;color:var(--hint);letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap}
.nav-progress{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;flex-shrink:0}
.done-badge{font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;background:var(--surface2);color:var(--hint);padding:3px 10px;border-radius:20px;border:1px solid var(--border)}
.nav-home-btn{font-size:12px;padding:5px 12px;border-radius:20px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:transparent;color:var(--muted);cursor:pointer;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;display:none}
.nav-home-btn:hover{background:var(--surface2)}

/* ── VIEWS ── */
.view{display:none;max-width:700px;margin:0 auto;padding:1.25rem 1rem}
.view.active{display:block}

/* ── HOME ── */
.hero{margin-bottom:1.25rem}
.hero-title{font-size:22px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:.4rem;line-height:1.3}
.hero-sub{font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6}
.meta-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:8px;margin-bottom:1.25rem}
.meta-card{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:.75rem;text-align:center}
.meta-label{font-size:11px;color:var(--hint);margin-bottom:4px;font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:.04em}
.meta-val{font-size:20px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text)}

.filter-row{display:flex;gap:6px;overflow-x:auto;padding-bottom:4px;margin-bottom:.75rem;scrollbar-width:none}
.filter-row::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}
.fchip{flex-shrink:0;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;padding:5px 12px;border-radius:20px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface2);color:var(--muted);cursor:pointer;white-space:nowrap;transition:all .15s;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif}
.fchip.active{background:var(--text);color:var(--bg);border-color:var(--text)}

.sc-list{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px}
.sc-card{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);padding:1rem 1.25rem;cursor:pointer;transition:border-color .15s;display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:12px}
.sc-card:hover{border-color:var(--border2)}
.sc-card.hidden{display:none}
.sc-num{width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--surface2);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--muted);flex-shrink:0;transition:all .15s}
.sc-num.done{background:var(--station-bg);color:var(--station)}
.sc-body{flex:1;min-width:0}
.sc-title{font-size:14px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:3px;line-height:1.3}
.sc-meta{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.mod-tag{font-size:10px;font-weight:500;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:20px;font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;white-space:nowrap}
.sc-note{font-size:11px;color:var(--hint)}
.sc-arrow{color:var(--hint);font-size:16px;flex-shrink:0;align-self:center}

/* ── STATION ── */
.timer-bar{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin-bottom:.75rem}
.timer-row{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:.6rem}
.phase-pill{font-size:11px;font-weight:500;padding:3px 10px;border-radius:20px;font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;letter-spacing:.04em}
.phase-pill.reading{background:var(--reading-bg);color:var(--reading)}
.phase-pill.station{background:var(--station-bg);color:var(--station)}
.timer-digits{font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:28px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text);letter-spacing:.05em;transition:color .3s}
.timer-digits.warn{color:var(--warn)}
.timer-digits.danger{color:var(--danger)}
.progress-track{width:100%;height:3px;background:var(--surface3);border-radius:2px;overflow:hidden}
.progress-fill{height:100%;border-radius:2px;transition:width .8s linear,background .3s}
.progress-fill.reading{background:var(--reading)}
.progress-fill.station{background:var(--station)}
.progress-fill.warn{background:var(--warn)}
.progress-fill.danger{background:var(--danger)}

.phase-note{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);background:var(--surface2);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:.6rem .9rem;margin-bottom:.75rem;line-height:1.5;border-left:2px solid var(--border2)}

.scenario-card{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);padding:1.25rem;margin-bottom:.75rem}
.scenario-eyebrow{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:.75rem}
.scenario-label{font-size:10px;font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;color:var(--hint);letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase}
.scenario-text{font-size:14px;line-height:1.75;color:var(--text)}

.qs-card{background:var(--surface2);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:1rem;margin-bottom:.75rem}
.qs-label{font-size:10px;font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;color:var(--hint);letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:.6rem}
.q-item{font-size:14px;color:var(--text);line-height:1.65;display:flex;gap:.6rem;margin-bottom:.5rem}
.q-item:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
.q-n{font-family:'DM Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;color:var(--hint);flex-shrink:0;padding-top:2px}

.hints-row{margin-bottom:.75rem}
.hints-toggle-btn{font-size:12px;color:var(--hint);background:transparent;border:none;cursor:pointer;padding:0;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}
.hints-panel{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);padding:.9rem;margin-top:.5rem;display:none}
.hint-row{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;padding:.2rem 0;padding-left:1.1rem;position:relative}
.hint-row::before{content:"→";position:absolute;left:0;color:var(--hint);font-size:11px}

.station-btns{display:flex;gap:8px}
.btn{padding:10px 16px;font-size:14px;font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif;border-radius:var(--radius);cursor:pointer;transition:all .15s;border:1px solid var(--border)}
.btn-main{flex:1;font-weight:500;background:var(--surface);color:var(--text)}
.btn-main:hover{background:var(--surface2)}
.btn-leave{background:transparent;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}
.btn-leave:hover{border-color:var(--border2);color:var(--text)}

/* ── REVIEW ── */
.review-header{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);padding:1.25rem;margin-bottom:.75rem}
.review-title{font-size:18px;font-weight:500;margin-bottom:.3rem}
.review-sub{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted)}
.model-section{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);padding:1.25rem;margin-bottom:.75rem}
.model-heading{font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:.5rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem}
.model-heading::before{content:'';width:3px;height:14px;border-radius:2px;background:var(--station);flex-shrink:0}
.model-body{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75}
.review-btns{display:flex;gap:8px}
.btn-next{flex:1;font-weight:500;background:var(--text);color:var(--bg);border-color:var(--text)}
.btn-next:hover{opacity:.85}
.btn-home-r{background:transparent;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}
.btn-home-r:hover{border-color:var(--border2);color:var(--text)}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<nav>
  <span class="nav-title">FYA Practice Stations</span>
  <div class="nav-progress">
    <span class="done-badge" id="doneBadge">0 / 13 done</span>
    <button class="nav-home-btn" id="navHomeBtn" onclick="goHome()">← Home</button>
  </div>
</nav>

<!-- HOME -->
<div class="view active" id="homeView">
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-title">Practice stations</div>
    <div class="hero-sub">13 scenarios across all 6 modules. Each station: 3 min reading, 9 min answering — matching the real FYA format. Select any scenario to begin.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="meta-grid">
    <div class="meta-card"><div class="meta-label">Scenarios</div><div class="meta-val">13</div></div>
    <div class="meta-card"><div class="meta-label">Reading</div><div class="meta-val">3 min</div></div>
    <div class="meta-card"><div class="meta-label">Station</div><div class="meta-val">9 min</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="filter-row" id="filterRow"></div>
  <div class="sc-list" id="scList"></div>
</div>

<!-- STATION -->
<div class="view" id="stationView">
  <div class="timer-bar">
    <div class="timer-row">
      <span class="phase-pill reading" id="phasePill">Reading</span>
      <span class="timer-digits" id="timerDigits">3:00</span>
    </div>
    <div class="progress-track"><div class="progress-fill reading" id="progressFill" style="width:100%"></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="phase-note" id="phaseNote"></div>
  <div class="scenario-card">
    <div class="scenario-eyebrow">
      <span class="scenario-label">Scenario <span id="scNumLabel"></span> of 13</span>
      <span class="mod-tag" id="scModTag"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="scenario-text" id="scText"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="qs-card">
    <div class="qs-label">Questions</div>
    <div id="qItems"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="hints-row">
    <button class="hints-toggle-btn" id="hintsToggleBtn" onclick="toggleHints()">Show curriculum pointers ↓</button>
    <div class="hints-panel" id="hintsPanel"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="station-btns">
    <button class="btn btn-main" id="mainBtn" onclick="handleMainBtn()">Start station</button>
    <button class="btn btn-leave" onclick="goHome()">Leave station</button>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- REVIEW -->
<div class="view" id="reviewView">
  <div class="review-header">
    <div class="review-title" id="reviewTitle"></div>
    <div class="review-sub" id="reviewSub"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="modelSections"></div>
  <div class="review-btns">
    <button class="btn btn-next" id="nextBtn" onclick="nextScenario()">Next scenario →</button>
    <button class="btn btn-home-r" onclick="goHome()">← Home</button>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
const MOD_STYLES={
  "Professional Foundations":"prof",
  "Data Science & Engineering":"ds",
  "Systems Development":"sys",
  "Policy & Strategy":"pol",
  "Digital Health & CDS":"dh",
  "Artificial Intelligence":"ai"
};

const SCENARIOS=[
  {
    module:"Professional Foundations",
    title:"A colleague raises a patient safety concern",
    tip:"Shortlisted by trainee above",
    text:"You are a newly registered Clinical Scientist in a Clinical Informatics team. During a team meeting, a junior colleague tells you privately that she has noticed a recurring data entry error in the EPR system causing patients to receive incorrect medication dose alerts. She is worried about raising it formally because her previous manager dismissed similar concerns. She asks for your advice.",
    qs:["What are your professional and ethical obligations in this situation, and how would you advise your colleague?","What processes and structures exist within the NHS to support the raising of patient safety concerns?"],
    hints:["Duty of candour (Regulation 20) — statutory, organisational and professional obligation","HCPC Standards of Conduct 7: raise concerns about safety — not optional","Freedom to Speak Up Guardians: statutory role post-Francis Report 2013","LFPSE (Learning from Patient Safety Events): replaced STEIS for NHS England","PSIRF 2022 (Patient Safety Incident Response Framework): proportionate investigation","Psychological safety and organisational culture","Your scope of practice: escalate, don't investigate alone"],
    model:[
      {h:"Professional obligations",b:"As a registered Clinical Scientist, HCPC Standards of Conduct Standard 7 places a clear obligation to raise and act on concerns about safety — this is not discretionary. I would explain this to my colleague and reassure her that raising this concern is both her right and her professional duty."},
      {h:"Immediate steps",b:"I would advise her to document what she has observed with specific dates and episode references where possible — factually and without speculation. Contemporaneous records are important if the concern is later investigated. I would offer to support her rather than asking her to act alone."},
      {h:"Escalation pathways",b:"The incident should be logged on the trust's LFPSE system. If she has concerns about departmental culture preventing escalation, she can approach the Freedom to Speak Up Guardian — a statutory, independent and confidential role. She is legally protected from detriment under the Public Interest Disclosure Act 1998."},
      {h:"Clinical governance structures",b:"The trust's clinical governance framework — risk management, incident review, and the PSIRF — exists precisely for this situation. The Clinical Informatics team lead and Caldicott Guardian should be informed if patient-identifiable data has been compromised. The error may require root cause analysis and a CAPA process under the team's QMS."},
      {h:"Culture",b:"I would validate my colleague's concern and acknowledge the psychological safety dimension. The NHS People Promise and NHS Constitution both commit to an environment where staff can raise concerns without fear of reprisal."}
    ]
  },
  {
    module:"Digital Health & CDS",
    title:"Deploying an AI triage tool in the ED",
    text:"Your trust is planning to deploy an AI-based triage decision support tool in the Emergency Department. The tool was developed by a private company and uses historical ED attendance data to predict patient acuity and recommend triage categories. The Head of Emergency Medicine has asked your Clinical Informatics team to lead the evaluation and governance sign-off process before go-live.",
    qs:["What evaluation and governance processes would you apply before recommending the tool for deployment?","What specific risks would you want to assess, and how would you monitor the tool's performance after go-live?"],
    hints:["SaMD: likely Class IIa under UK MDR 2002 — requires UKCA marking and technical file","DTAC: six domains — clinical safety, data protection, technical security, interoperability, usability, equality","DCB0129 (manufacturer) and DCB0160 (deployment) clinical safety standards","NICE Evidence Standards Framework for DHTs: Tier C evidence for clinical pathway tools","Algorithmic bias: historical ED data may under-represent certain demographics","Automation bias: clinicians over-rely on output under pressure","Post-market surveillance: monitor for model drift, subgroup performance","Alert fatigue if tool generates frequent low-confidence outputs"],
    model:[
      {h:"Regulatory status",b:"The tool performs a medical purpose and is therefore Software as a Medical Device (SaMD) under UK MDR 2002, likely Class IIa or higher. I would request the manufacturer's technical file, Declaration of Conformity, and UKCA marking documentation before any further evaluation."},
      {h:"Clinical safety standards",b:"DCB0129 (manufacturer clinical risk) and DCB0160 (deployment clinical risk management) must both be met. I would work with our Clinical Safety Officer to complete a deployment hazard assessment and safety case report before go-live."},
      {h:"DTAC assessment",b:"I would conduct a DTAC review across all six domains: clinical safety, data protection, technical security, interoperability with our EPR, usability/accessibility, and equality and inclusion. Any gaps must be resolved prior to deployment."},
      {h:"Evidence appraisal",b:"I would review validation evidence against the NICE Evidence Standards Framework for DHTs. For a tool influencing clinical pathways I would want Tier C evidence — patient outcome benefit — and check whether validation was performed in a comparable NHS ED population."},
      {h:"Bias and fairness",b:"Historical ED triage data may encode systematic biases. I would audit performance across age, sex, ethnicity, and deprivation before go-live."},
      {h:"Post-market surveillance",b:"After deployment I would establish a monitoring dashboard: triage accuracy vs outcome, override rates (high rates may indicate automation bias), subgroup performance, and model drift over time. Pre-defined thresholds would trigger formal review or suspension."}
    ]
  },
  {
    module:"Data Science & Engineering",
    title:"A data breach in a research project",
    text:"You are a Clinical Informatician on a population cohort study linking primary and secondary care data. During a routine review you discover that a dataset containing NHS numbers, dates of birth, and GP practice codes has been shared with an external academic partner without a data sharing agreement in place, contrary to the project's information governance approvals.",
    qs:["What are your immediate obligations under data protection law and NHS information governance frameworks?","What steps would you take to manage and learn from this incident?"],
    hints:["UK GDPR Article 33: notify ICO within 72 hours if breach likely to result in risk to individuals","UK GDPR Article 34: notify affected individuals if high risk","NHS numbers + DoB = personal data; likely special category health data","Caldicott Principles 1, 2, 6: justified purpose, minimum necessary, comply with law","DSPT: breaches must be reported and documented","Data Controller vs Data Processor: who bears responsibility?","Root cause analysis and CAPA to prevent recurrence","Research Ethics Committee: may need to be informed"],
    model:[
      {h:"Immediate containment",b:"My first obligation is to contain the breach — contact the external partner immediately and request the data be quarantined and not further processed or shared. Simultaneously notify the Data Protection Officer (DPO) and Caldicott Guardian, as NHS numbers and dates of birth constitute patient-identifiable health data (special category under GDPR Article 9)."},
      {h:"ICO notification",b:"Under UK GDPR Article 33, if the breach is likely to result in risk to individuals' rights and freedoms, the trust as Data Controller must notify the ICO within 72 hours of becoming aware. Notification must describe the nature of the breach, categories and approximate number of data subjects, likely consequences, and measures taken."},
      {h:"Individual notification",b:"If the breach creates high risk to individuals — for example if the data could identify patients with stigmatised conditions — Article 34 requires direct notification to those affected. The DPO and Senior Information Risk Owner (SIRO) must make this decision with legal advice."},
      {h:"Root cause and governance review",b:"A root cause analysis should identify why the data sharing agreement was missed. Was there a process gap, unclear responsibility, or inadequate training? Findings feed into a CAPA and update to the data management plan. The research sponsor and Research Ethics Committee should also be notified."},
      {h:"Learning and prevention",b:"The incident is logged on the DSPT and in the trust's incident management system. Systemic preventive actions: mandatory data sharing agreement verification before any transfer, clearer escalation pathways for researchers, and refreshed IG training aligned with Caldicott Principles."}
    ]
  },
  {
    module:"Systems Development",
    title:"An EPR implementation going off-track",
    text:"Your NHS trust is 6 months into a 2-year EPR implementation. Reports from clinical departments show very low end-user engagement, clinical workflows have not been correctly mapped, and there are concerns that data migration from the legacy system contains errors affecting patient record accuracy. The Project Board has asked your team for a briefing on the issues and proposed actions.",
    qs:["How would you diagnose and prioritise the problems in this implementation?","What approaches would you recommend to get it back on track?"],
    hints:["Lessons from NPFIT: engagement failure and requirements drift are the most common causes of NHS IT project failure","Systems thinking: sociotechnical system — people, process, and technology together","Workflow mapping must precede system configuration, not follow it","Data migration: validation against source system, parallel running, sample-based audit","Change management: Kotter's 8 steps — is there coalition, urgency, communication?","PRINCE2: exception reporting, change control, updated risk register","Clinical champions programme for UAT","Patient safety: migration errors could cause direct harm — highest priority"],
    model:[
      {h:"Diagnosing the problems",b:"The issues fall into three categories: a people/engagement problem (insufficient clinical co-design), a process problem (workflows configured to an incorrect specification), and a data quality problem (migration errors that will persist into the new system). All three must be addressed in parallel, not sequence."},
      {h:"Prioritisation: data migration",b:"Migration errors are the highest priority due to direct patient safety risk — incorrect historical records could lead to wrong clinical decisions. I would recommend pausing further migration until a systematic data quality assessment, including sample-based validation against source records, is complete."},
      {h:"Clinical engagement",b:"I would establish or reinvigorate a clinical champions programme with engaged clinicians in each specialty. Workflow mapping workshops — led by clinical staff, not just observed by IT — should be run before any reconfiguration. UAT scripts should be co-designed with clinical users."},
      {h:"Change management",b:"Using Kotter's framework: I would assess whether there is sufficient urgency, executive-level sponsorship visible to frontline staff, a clear vision of what the EPR will enable, and quick wins to rebuild confidence. Communication failure is often as significant as technical failure."},
      {h:"Governance escalation",b:"Under PRINCE2, the accumulation of issues — scope deviation, risk materialisation — must be escalated to the Project Board as an exception report. The risk register should be updated and change control applied before any timeline or scope changes are agreed."}
    ]
  },
  {
    module:"Policy & Strategy",
    title:"Population health analytics dashboard for an ICB",
    text:"Your Integrated Care Board wants to commission a population health analytics dashboard to identify patients at high risk of hospital admission so community teams can intervene proactively. The tool will use linked primary and secondary care data and be accessible to GPs, community nurses, and social care teams across the ICB footprint. Your Clinical Informatics team is leading development.",
    qs:["What strategic and governance considerations must you address before development begins?","How would you ensure the tool does not exacerbate existing health inequalities?"],
    hints:["ICS structure: ICB (NHS commissioning) and ICP (includes social care) — cross-boundary data sharing requires formal agreements","Data Saves Lives strategy: SDE principles, FDP for operational data","UK GDPR lawful basis: Article 6(1)(e) public task + Article 9(2)(h) for health data","Caldicott Principles: justified purpose, minimum necessary","DSPT current for all partner organisations","Health inequalities: Core20PLUS5 — target most deprived 20% and clinical priority areas","Algorithmic bias: under-served groups may have sparser data → underestimated risk","NASSS framework: assess complexity across seven domains before build","DTAC if algorithmic risk scores influence clinical decisions (SaMD boundary)"],
    model:[
      {h:"Strategic context",b:"This initiative sits within NHS England's 'hospital to community' shift and the Data Saves Lives strategy. The ICB has statutory population health responsibility under the Health and Care Act 2022. I would ensure clear strategic mandate, executive sponsorship from both NHS and local authority partners, and a shared vision agreed across organisational boundaries."},
      {h:"Information governance",b:"Linking primary and secondary care data requires formal data sharing agreements between all organisations before any data flows. The lawful basis is likely Article 6(1)(e) public task with Article 9(2)(h) safeguards. The Caldicott Guardian must approve data uses, and DSPT must be current for all data-accessing organisations. SDE principles should apply — no bulk transfers, access within a controlled environment where possible."},
      {h:"SaMD boundary",b:"If the dashboard includes an algorithmic risk score that clinicians use to prioritise patients, this may constitute SaMD under UK MDR 2002. I would seek MHRA guidance and, if SaMD classification applies, complete DTAC assessment and DCB0160 clinical risk management before deployment."},
      {h:"Health inequalities",b:"Risk models trained on NHS data encode existing inequalities — patients from deprived areas and some ethnic minority groups have sparser records, leading to underestimated risk scores. I would explicitly evaluate model performance across Core20PLUS5 dimensions and require subgroup fairness analysis as part of governance sign-off."},
      {h:"Stakeholder engagement",b:"GPs and community nurses are high power / high interest — their co-design involvement is essential. Social care colleagues bring different data governance frameworks; early joint workshops will surface interoperability and consent challenges. Patient representatives, especially from communities likely to be targeted, should be involved from the start."}
    ]
  },
  {
    module:"Artificial Intelligence",
    title:"Critically appraising an AI retinopathy screening model",
